## Engineering practices

{{APPLICABLE_ENGINEERING_RULES_AND_LANGUAGE_SPECIFICS}}

Follow this repository's established practices by default. Support claims that
a practice is wrong or unsuitable with a concrete local problem and applicable
project or authoritative reference documentation. Explain the scoped alternative,
tradeoffs and verification; distinguish requirements from recommendations and
facts from assumptions. Unsupported preferences do not justify replacing a
convention. Evidence does not override active instructions or delivery authority.

Before implementing a new capability, resolve what the requirement actually
means (granularity, volume, time, identity, consumers, failure behaviour),
compare at least two genuinely different designs with the cost each hides, and
classify the chosen one as easy or expensive to reverse. Cheap-to-undo choices
need only a recorded note; expensive-to-undo ones need the alternatives and the
owner's decision before code is written.

