## Git and delivery

{{AUTHORIZED_ACTIONS_AND_REQUIRED_DECISIONS}}

Preserve unrelated work and inspect the intended diff before staging. Keep
implementation edits in the contract's workspace; review and verify the final
change before the permitted delivery step. Do not bypass blocking hooks.
Local integration, remote publication and release follow their declared
authority and gates, including CI actions triggered by a push or merge.

## Task state and handoff

{{TRACKER_LOCATION_BOOTSTRAP_AND_TEAM_RECORD_BINDING}}

When external-to-local execution mapping is explicitly enabled, map each
participating ticket to one canonical local task using scoped stable identity.
An external tracker alone does not require a second local task record.
For full dev-flow execution, Beads is the primary tracker; external systems are
optional linked representations. Record canonical task decisions and evidence
in Beads. Reuse existing mappings and report pending/conflicting updates;
remote writes require their own authority.

Resume from the task record and actual checkout state. Record acceptance
criteria, task type and the applicable initial design or diagnosis before
implementation planning; keep unresolved phase decisions explicit. Record
evidence, the tested revision/environment, delivery state, remaining work and
the next action in the chosen tracker. Report retained worktrees or data with
their location and reason; close only when the requested acceptance is met.
